              "description": "Backdrive force is a mechanical transparency measure from the fingertip to the actuators defined as the smallest force imposed at the fingertip that causes motion at the actuators. This property can be tested by pressing on the fingertip with a slowly increasing force while measuring the actuator positions. Once motion is detected at the actuators, the fingertip force is recorded as the backdrive force.",
